From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 04:47:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(providers): Claude accounts that share sessions through
 account tokens

Carried on custom while the design is discussed on upstream issue #503;
see docs/providers.md. Drop it once upstream has an equivalent.

An account with its own config_dir also gets its own transcripts, settings,
skills and plugins, so a conversation started on one Claude account cannot
continue on another without moving files, and the accounts drift apart.

A claude subscription entry now accepts token_ref, an env: or keychain:
reference to a `claude setup-token` token. Claude reads it from
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN, which takes precedence over the login stored in its
config directory, so token accounts share one ~/.claude and differ only in
which subscription pays:

- The runner resolves the token itself and passes it only to the Claude
  process: the native terminal's env, or the claude-sdk spawn env. It never
  enters the runner's environment or the host launch frame.
- The account is the agent's pinned provider, else the session's choice or
  the host default. A missing token fails the launch with the command that
  creates one, and a startup command or agent env that replaces the token
  fails instead of running on another account.
- A token account counts as signed in when its token resolves, for the host
  provider listing, readiness and launch checks.
- `omnigent setup` can add a token account (paste the token; it is stored in
  the Omnigent secret store). Removing one deletes its token and never runs
  `claude auth logout`, which would sign out the shared login.
- Picker labels no longer include login directories.

Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Docs: none (documented with its series in docs/providers.md)
